01:16:43,529 --> 01:16:45,117
-Fats, you better
go get the money.

1911
01:16:45,152 --> 01:16:46,394
-It's code.

1912
01:16:46,429 --> 01:16:48,949
-I want firm tummies and a nice,straight dance line.

1913
01:16:48,983 --> 01:16:50,260
Come on.

1914
01:16:50,295 --> 01:16:52,331
-You get this.

1915
01:16:52,366 --> 01:16:54,644
-Oh, great. There's stamps
and some paper clips

1916
01:16:54,679 --> 01:16:56,094
and a Garfield sticker and --

1917
01:16:56,128 --> 01:16:58,199
Hey, grab that statue that says
"World's Greatest Grandma."

1918
01:16:58,234 --> 01:16:59,753
-Hey, look -- $10!

1919
01:16:59,787 --> 01:17:00,995
Hey, we're set
for the rest of our lives,

1920
01:17:01,030 --> 01:17:03,446
unless we want to buy
a 12-pack or something.

1921
01:17:03,480 --> 01:17:05,897
-Hey, they play The Ventures
at this bank.

1922
01:17:05,931 --> 01:17:07,588
-Wow, they got everything --

1923
01:17:07,623 --> 01:17:09,694
stadium blanket, calendar,
Lincoln coin bank.

1924
01:17:09,728 --> 01:17:11,350
-Mm. Oh.

1925
01:17:11,385 --> 01:17:12,938
-Look at the bank sign.

1926
01:17:12,973 --> 01:17:15,113
It's printed with electrician's
tape on ceiling tile.

1927
01:17:15,147 --> 01:17:16,355
-I'm thinking of
growing a Van Dyke.

1928
01:17:16,390 --> 01:17:18,703
What do you think, huh?
Yeah.

1929
01:17:18,737 --> 01:17:21,326
-Did you see "Cop Rock"
last night?

1930
01:17:21,360 --> 01:17:23,155
It sucked.

1931
01:17:24,501 --> 01:17:26,987
-Hmm.

1932
01:17:27,021 --> 01:17:29,645
Now, if I could just remember
my Aldis code from the Navy.

1933
01:17:29,679 --> 01:17:32,199
-Hey, what's with the lights?

1934
01:17:32,233 --> 01:17:34,166
-What about them?
-Hmm.

1935
01:17:34,201 --> 01:17:35,581
Whoa. Your brights.

1936
01:17:35,616 --> 01:17:37,860
-Hey, man,
he's doing Aldis code.

1937
01:17:40,483 --> 01:17:42,692
-Help. Help.
-Hey, hey, help us.

1938
01:17:42,727 --> 01:17:44,694
-Help.
-Looks like he's trying
to signal us.

1939
01:17:44,729 --> 01:17:46,662
-Oh, no, he's just
testing his lights.

1940
01:17:46,696 --> 01:17:50,148
Let's go dunk a couple
of spudnuts, eh, Phil?

1941
01:17:50,182 --> 01:17:51,632
-Hey, is that their car?

1942
01:17:51,667 --> 01:17:53,461
Sounds like they got
a tappet loose.

1943
01:17:53,496 --> 01:17:55,222
-Yeah.

1944
01:17:56,568 --> 01:17:58,604
-That's better.

1945
01:17:58,639 --> 01:18:01,159
-Eh, what's all this, then?

1946
01:18:01,193 --> 01:18:03,471
I mean, what's going on here,
boy?

1947
01:18:06,302 --> 01:18:08,304
-Well, son,
what's the lights for?

1948
01:18:08,338 --> 01:18:10,099
-Uh, illuminating the road
after dark, sir.

1949
01:18:10,133 --> 01:18:11,721
-There's three men and a girl
robbing that bank.

1950
01:18:11,756 --> 01:18:13,723
-And a baby.
-And a baby.

1951
01:18:13,758 --> 01:18:15,621
-Jeeter, it's the gestapo,
and they're talking to Rod.

1952
01:18:15,656 --> 01:18:17,658
Let's split!
-No. You'rethe gestapo.

1953
01:18:17,693 --> 01:18:19,453
-Linda, Fats, stand up!

1954
01:18:19,487 --> 01:18:21,386
Let's go!
-This better not be a joke.

1955
01:18:21,420 --> 01:18:22,836
-Well, it is a joke,
but it's still true.

1956
01:18:22,870 --> 01:18:24,527
-You stay put, kid.

1957
01:18:26,494 --> 01:18:29,221
-Here we go.
Hmm.

1958
01:18:29,256 --> 01:18:31,051
-Whoa, that's a nice
wide spread.

1959
01:18:31,085 --> 01:18:32,949
He must have had
a modified choke on that.

1960
01:18:32,984 --> 01:18:34,710
Hmm.
-Fats, we just hit
a couple of the fuzz.

1961
01:18:34,744 --> 01:18:36,263
-Huh?
-What?

1962
01:18:38,990 --> 01:18:40,646
-Oh.

1963
01:18:40,681 --> 01:18:43,304
-Hold it, creep,
or I'll blow your brains out.

1964
01:18:43,339 --> 01:18:45,237
-Yeah.
-Come on. Move!

1965
01:18:45,272 --> 01:18:46,963
Linda, hurry up!
-Linda!

1966
01:18:46,998 --> 01:18:49,276
-In these heels? Are you crazy?
-Fats, move it!

1967
01:18:52,382 --> 01:18:54,108
-Ohh!
-Okay, coming boss.

1968
01:18:54,143 --> 01:18:56,352
-Nice tag.

1969
01:18:56,386 --> 01:18:57,836
[Alarm rings]

1970
01:18:57,871 --> 01:19:00,459
-Oh, school's out.
Recess, everybody.

1971
01:19:00,494 --> 01:19:02,496
[Ringing continues]

1972
01:19:05,292 --> 01:19:07,604
-Okay, now, we all saw
the Zapruder film.

1973
01:19:07,639 --> 01:19:10,538
You be Kennedy.
-He signaled the men.

1974
01:19:10,573 --> 01:19:12,678
-[Speaks indistinctly]
-Hmm?

1975
01:19:12,713 --> 01:19:14,646
-What?
-What?

1976
01:19:14,680 --> 01:19:16,682
-Man, that wasn't
a very nice thing to do.

1977
01:19:16,717 --> 01:19:19,824
-If Banjo's telling the truth,
why don't we just dump him now?

1978
01:19:19,858 --> 01:19:22,136
-'Cause this creep is gonnaget us away from the little men.

1979
01:19:22,171 --> 01:19:24,449
-Mm.
-He's gonna drive the race
of his life.

1980
01:19:24,483 --> 01:19:27,107
Put your foot to the floorboard,man. Move it.

1981
01:19:27,141 --> 01:19:29,281
I said move it!
-But remember your seat belt.

1982
01:19:29,316 --> 01:19:31,421
Check your blind spot.
Three-point check.

1983
01:19:31,456 --> 01:19:33,251
That's better. Thank you.
-No, not this way, man.

1984
01:19:33,285 --> 01:19:35,736
My mom will see me. Ohh!

1985
01:19:37,048 --> 01:19:40,189
-Come on, man! Earn your money.
Faster. Faster.

1986
01:19:40,223 --> 01:19:41,846
[Ringing continues]

1987
01:19:41,880 --> 01:19:43,640
-Ohh.

1988
01:19:43,675 --> 01:19:45,850
-Oh, you poor officer.

1989
01:19:45,884 --> 01:19:48,818
Oh.
Can I get you a doughnut?

1990
01:19:48,853 --> 01:19:52,166
-Ugh.
You're kneeling on my chest.
-Help me to my car.

1991
01:19:52,201 --> 01:19:54,997
-I'm sorry, but you're dead.

1992
01:19:55,031 --> 01:19:57,102
No doughnuts.

1993
01:19:57,137 --> 01:19:59,277
-Hmm. Poor guy.

1994
01:19:59,311 --> 01:20:00,968
-Yep.

1995
01:20:01,003 --> 01:20:02,659
-Mayday! Mayday!

1996
01:20:02,694 --> 01:20:05,662
-He used to be a pilot.
-I used too much rouge!

1997
01:20:05,697 --> 01:20:09,011
-Four men and a girl just robbedthe Citrusville bank.

1998
01:20:09,045 --> 01:20:13,084
-507 to all units,
507 to all units.

1999
01:20:13,118 --> 01:20:14,602
Whatever your location,

2000
01:20:14,637 --> 01:20:17,088
proceed to roadblock stations
around Citrusville.

2001
01:20:17,122 --> 01:20:18,641
-Uh, we are all the units, sir.

2002
01:20:18,675 --> 01:20:21,817
-Proceed to roadblock stations
around Citrusville.

2003
01:20:21,851 --> 01:20:24,889
-Heh. They're gonna put the
squeeze on them in Citrusville.

2004
01:20:24,923 --> 01:20:28,685
-Nelson Riddle
and his Orchestra!

2005
01:20:28,720 --> 01:20:31,274
-"Squeeze on them." See?
-Yeah. We got it, bro.

2006
01:20:31,309 --> 01:20:33,829
-What's, uh, Citrusville
famous for, you suppose?

2007
01:20:33,863 --> 01:20:35,865
-Uh, probably dairy products.
-I wa-- Huh?

2008
01:20:35,900 --> 01:20:36,866
-Yeah?

2009
01:20:36,901 --> 01:20:39,420
-Police cars
courtesy of Grandma.

2010
01:20:42,665 --> 01:20:45,426
-You're doing great, baby.
-Don't call me that at work.

2011
01:20:45,461 --> 01:20:47,739
-Hey, that looks like the car.
-Naw!

2012
01:20:47,773 --> 01:20:49,534
Couldn't be. They're miles away.-Get ready. Here they come.

2013
01:20:49,568 --> 01:20:50,742
-Oh, no.
[Gunfire]

2014
01:20:50,776 --> 01:20:54,125
-Ayyy-ahhhhh!

2015
01:20:54,159 --> 01:20:55,574
-Ugh!
-Ohh!
-Ooh.

2016
01:20:55,609 --> 01:20:57,300
-That'll teach 'em. Whoa.

2017
01:20:57,335 --> 01:20:59,544
[Tires screeching]

2018
01:21:01,442 --> 01:21:04,411
-Ooh!
-Oh, Calgon, take me away!

2019
01:21:05,826 --> 01:21:08,346
-I got one in my hair!
Crawlers!

2020
01:21:08,380 --> 01:21:09,865
-Yeah, man.
-Stupid old bun.

2021
01:21:09,899 --> 01:21:12,833
-I love it.
Another one for me.

2022
01:21:12,868 --> 01:21:14,835
-You know, this really is
kind of fun.

2023
01:21:14,870 --> 01:21:16,319
-Whoo-hoo.

2024
01:21:19,046 --> 01:21:22,429
-I'm having a really good time.
-Yeah.

2025
01:21:22,463 --> 01:21:24,672
-I'll get a Kleenex, Bob.
Stay there.

2026
01:21:26,743 --> 01:21:28,124
-Officer down, officer down.

2027
01:21:28,159 --> 01:21:29,850
I need bear claws --
I mean, uh, backup.

2028
01:21:29,885 --> 01:21:32,646
Send a jelly doughnut.
Uh, I mean send help.

2029
01:21:32,680 --> 01:21:35,407
-Gang headed East
on Old Citrus Road.

2030
01:21:35,442 --> 01:21:37,478
Just killed my partner.
-And I'm all busted up inside.

2031
01:21:37,513 --> 01:21:38,928
Over.
-I'm in pursuit.

2032
01:21:38,963 --> 01:21:40,965
[Siren wailing]
-Here comes the fuzz!

2033
01:21:40,999 --> 01:21:42,967
-Here comes the fuzz!
Here comes the fuzz!

2034
01:21:43,001 --> 01:21:45,210
-Da fuzz is comin'.
-Yeah.

2035
01:21:45,245 --> 01:21:48,006
-Yeah. Hey,
he's doing really well.

2036
01:21:48,041 --> 01:21:49,766
-Yeah, this is the longest
he's driven

2037
01:21:49,801 --> 01:21:51,527
without rolling and burning.
-[Laughs]

2038
01:21:51,561 --> 01:21:53,529
-Another roadblock!

2039
01:21:53,563 --> 01:21:55,324
Drive through it, man.
Drive through it.

2040
01:21:55,358 --> 01:21:57,705
-Yeah. Whoa.

2041
01:21:57,740 --> 01:21:59,776
-Oh, you know,
we really should have

2042
01:21:59,811 --> 01:22:01,226
blocked the other road, too.

2043
01:22:01,261 --> 01:22:02,572
What were we thinking?

2044
01:22:02,607 --> 01:22:04,436
-Roadblock detour.

2045
01:22:04,471 --> 01:22:06,645
-Down the Yellow Brick Road,
man.

2046
01:22:06,680 --> 01:22:09,614
-Guess we're not in Kansas
anymore, dude.

2047
01:22:09,648 --> 01:22:11,236
Go kill Dorothy.

2048
01:22:11,271 --> 01:22:13,135
-Well, that's kind of like
closing the barn door

2049
01:22:13,169 --> 01:22:14,412
after the cows are out.

2050
01:22:14,446 --> 01:22:15,792
Come on, dummy.

2051
01:22:15,827 --> 01:22:17,622
-Uh, signal your turn, please.

2052
01:22:17,656 --> 01:22:19,382
Uh -- Oh, well.

2053
01:22:19,417 --> 01:22:22,247
[Tires screech, engine revs]

2054
01:22:22,282 --> 01:22:24,249
-What's he gonna do --
shoot at oranges?

2055
01:22:24,284 --> 01:22:26,286
-Looks like it.

2056
01:22:26,320 --> 01:22:28,529
[Sirens wailing, tires screech]

2057
01:22:28,564 --> 01:22:30,600
Oh, now, that's a fire siren.

2058
01:22:30,635 --> 01:22:32,499
Come on.

2059
01:22:32,533 --> 01:22:34,432
[Gunshot]

2060
01:22:34,466 --> 01:22:37,780
[Tires screeching]

2061
01:22:37,814 --> 01:22:40,231
I'm huge. I'm immense.

2062
01:22:40,265 --> 01:22:43,061
-Hey, look -- Erik Estrada!

2063
01:22:43,096 --> 01:22:44,200
[Gunshot]

2064
01:22:44,235 --> 01:22:46,582
-Slow 'em down, Banjo.

2065
01:22:46,616 --> 01:22:48,411
[Gunshot]

2066
01:22:48,446 --> 01:22:50,172
-Two barrels from Banjo
coming up!

2067
01:22:50,206 --> 01:22:52,036
-Did he say
"two bowels for Banjo?"

2068
01:22:52,070 --> 01:22:54,279
-"Bedtime for Banjo"?

2069
01:22:54,314 --> 01:22:58,076
-Would you get your arms and
legs inside this car, please?

2070
01:22:58,111 --> 01:23:00,596
-How am doing it?
I don't know.

2071
01:23:00,630 --> 01:23:02,529
-Whee, man, we were rolling.

2072
01:23:02,563 --> 01:23:06,774
-Gonna get some...
and some rolls and some....

2073
01:23:06,809 --> 01:23:08,224
Hey, hey, hey.

2074
01:23:08,259 --> 01:23:11,193
Every day, all my love away.
-I'm huge.

2075
01:23:11,227 --> 01:23:13,471
By this time,
the old Duke boys

2076
01:23:13,505 --> 01:23:16,094
had killed just about
every cop in town.
-Yee-hoo.

2077
01:23:16,129 --> 01:23:18,924
-And Daisy had slipped into
something more comfortable.

2078
01:23:18,959 --> 01:23:23,032
-Oh, it's a squealing swamp.
Oh, there's the exploding bush.

2079
01:23:23,067 --> 01:23:24,965
-Hmm.
-Earn your money.

2080
01:23:25,000 --> 01:23:26,932
Drive, baby, drive!

2081
01:23:26,967 --> 01:23:28,348
-What do you think I'm doing?!

2082
01:23:28,382 --> 01:23:31,109
Oh, look, I'm cranky and hungry.I'm sorry.

2083
01:23:32,352 --> 01:23:34,492
-Back into the squealing swamp.

2084
01:23:34,526 --> 01:23:35,941
-So, this is the point
where the director said,

2085
01:23:35,976 --> 01:23:37,426
"Use everything we shot."

2086
01:23:37,460 --> 01:23:38,875
-What's wrong with the car?
-Who's talking?

2087
01:23:38,910 --> 01:23:40,187
-Oh, they must have hit
the gas tank.

2088
01:23:40,222 --> 01:23:41,326
-Who's talking?

2089
01:23:41,361 --> 01:23:42,845
-I don't know.
-You see the lighthouse?

2090
01:23:42,879 --> 01:23:43,949
Stop there.

2091
01:23:43,984 --> 01:23:45,192
-Lighthouse?
They're in the woods.

2092
01:23:45,227 --> 01:23:47,919
-We're going down.
We've lost an engine.

2093
01:23:47,953 --> 01:23:50,059
-Lighthouse?

2094
01:23:50,094 --> 01:23:51,612
[Siren wailing]

2095
01:23:51,647 --> 01:23:53,373
-Oh, it's for Winnebagos.
-Mm.

2096
01:23:53,407 --> 01:23:55,340
-Yeah. Lighthouse.
-Well, it's up to the Navy now.

2097
01:23:55,375 --> 01:23:57,170
It's out of our jurisdiction.
-Whoa.

2098
01:23:57,204 --> 01:23:59,034
-Come on, baby. Move it!
-Whoa! That's too close.

2099
01:23:59,068 --> 01:24:01,243
-Mm.

2100
01:24:01,277 --> 01:24:03,279
-Stop calling me "baby."

2101
01:24:03,314 --> 01:24:05,454
[Gunshots]

2102
01:24:05,488 --> 01:24:07,766
-Oh, great hideout.

2103
01:24:07,801 --> 01:24:09,182
If they have to spend
any time there,

2104
01:24:09,216 --> 01:24:11,080
they can eat the bricks,
I guess.

2105
01:24:11,115 --> 01:24:13,117
-Oh, look, they're in
a nautilus, you guys.

2106
01:24:13,151 --> 01:24:15,222
-It's like "The Time Tunnel."

2107
01:24:15,257 --> 01:24:18,467
[Gunfire]

2108
01:24:18,501 --> 01:24:20,158
[Siren wailing]

2109
01:24:20,193 --> 01:24:22,436
-Don't shoot the car!
We need that!

2110
01:24:24,093 --> 01:24:25,922
-Ooh! Sorry.
I accidentally shot a cop.

2111
01:24:25,957 --> 01:24:27,683
Sorry.
-Load it up, Linda.

2112
01:24:27,717 --> 01:24:29,098
-It's just like shooting ducks
in an alley.

2113
01:24:29,133 --> 01:24:30,375
-I think it's
"fish in a barrel,"

2114
01:24:30,410 --> 01:24:31,514
but I know what you mean,

2115
01:24:31,549 --> 01:24:33,482
and you'll know what we mean
after this.

2116
01:24:33,516 --> 01:24:36,174
[Gunshots, siren wailing]

2117
01:24:36,209 --> 01:24:40,454
♪♪

2118
01:24:41,973 --> 01:24:45,149
[Gunshots]

2119
01:24:45,183 --> 01:24:47,634
-For the glory
of the SLA, Tania!

2120
01:24:47,668 --> 01:24:49,774
-I just got a thing
about girls with guns.

2121
01:24:49,808 --> 01:24:51,776
I don't know.
-Yeah.

2122
01:24:53,502 --> 01:24:55,090
-Hi.

2123
01:24:55,124 --> 01:24:57,782
-Here you go, Hoss.
Nice shootin', Little Joe.

2124
01:24:57,816 --> 01:24:59,059
-Oh.

2125
01:25:01,234 --> 01:25:03,063
Oh, my hair's stuck.
Ohh, ohh.

2126
01:25:03,098 --> 01:25:06,066
-I'm old enough to drive
and drink but not be in a war.

2127
01:25:06,101 --> 01:25:07,826
What do you think?

2128
01:25:07,861 --> 01:25:10,933
-Hey, it's Diana Rigg.

2129
01:25:10,967 --> 01:25:13,556
-Join us.

2130
01:25:13,591 --> 01:25:16,214
-Getting enough kicks now, baby?

2131
01:25:17,802 --> 01:25:19,528
Yeah.

2132
01:25:19,562 --> 01:25:21,288
[Gunfire]

2133
01:25:21,323 --> 01:25:23,635
If you've got something to say,
say it.

2134
01:25:27,570 --> 01:25:30,539
-You killed a tree, Banjo.

2135
01:25:30,573 --> 01:25:32,437
[Gunfire]

2136
01:25:32,472 --> 01:25:34,715
-Oh! Oh, oh! Oh, oh!
Excuse me.

2137
01:25:34,750 --> 01:25:37,270
-I got me one.
I got me a man.

2138
01:25:37,304 --> 01:25:39,651
-I'm happy for you.
Now go shoot cops.

2139
01:25:42,516 --> 01:25:45,070
-Quite a dance move there.

2140
01:25:46,900 --> 01:25:48,936
-Oh!
My head's trying to blow up!

2141
01:25:48,971 --> 01:25:50,559
-[Muttering]

2142
01:25:50,593 --> 01:25:52,216
-You idiot!
-He's wigging!

2143
01:25:52,250 --> 01:25:53,907
-Yep.

2144
01:25:53,941 --> 01:25:56,668
-Banjo, don't be a hero!
-Banjo, come back, you idiot!

2145
01:25:56,703 --> 01:25:58,153
-Come back, Banjo.
-Ohh!

2146
01:25:58,187 --> 01:26:00,396
-Whoa! Ouch!
-Stupid old gun.

2147
01:26:01,466 --> 01:26:03,468
-Cover him, Fats!
Cover him!

2148
01:26:05,884 --> 01:26:08,611
-Now, wait a minute. Banjo's
about two feet away from --

2149
01:26:08,646 --> 01:26:11,890
Look at that --
two feet away from the cops.

2150
01:26:11,925 --> 01:26:13,858
Criminy.

2151
01:26:13,892 --> 01:26:15,549
